# No end-of-line conversion, on anything.
#
# This tree is deliberately mixed: Cargo.toml, PERF.md and README.md are CRLF,
# while every .wgsl is LF and .rs and docs/ are LF with exactly three exceptions --
# src/lib.rs, src/stats.rs and docs/batch-11-godrays.md, which have been CRLF since
# before the tree went under version control. CLAUDE.md is a symlink to AGENTS.md
# (LF) since the 2026-09-18 documentation pass replaced the old CRLF briefing.
# Check the file before anchoring an edit on a newline rather than trusting the
# rule; batch 22 re-verified that the exception list is still complete and still
# three. Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would normalise the
# LF files to CRLF in the working copy on the next checkout and quietly rewrite most
# of the source tree. `-text` turns that off so the bytes in a clone are the bytes
# that were committed. Diffs are unaffected.
* -text
